      "c-OZPJ447gLD": {
        "value": "Unit of individuality"
      },
      "c-a5M1C6QnC0": {
        "value": "What is an “ant” — the nestmate, the colony, or something else? "
      },
      "c-ep6ISvxepn": {
        "value": {
          "root": {
            "children": [
              {
                "alignment": "Left",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Is the \"ant\" the nestmate? the colony? "
                  }
                ],
                "id": "cl-grid-n30XHRMvEl::i-jT6nwWh3ww::c-ep6ISvxepn-0",
                "lineLevel": 0,
                "style": "BulletedList",
                "type": "Line"
              },
              {
                "alignment": "Left",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Are ants social, eusocial, colonial, organismal, super-organismal, holo-organismal (e.g. symbionts, agriculture). "
                  }
                ],
                "id": "cl-Hlnc0CqfpF",
                "lineLevel": 0,
                "style": "BulletedList",
                "type": "Line"
              },
              {
                "alignment": "Left",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "What are the causes & consequences of “colony”? Other terms for this level of analysis? Just “ant” (as organism)?  "
                  }
